{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`review_plan_start(ticket)` returns a `job_id`; callers poll `gate_status(job_id)` and then read retained `REVIEW_RESULT` findings. The bug is that a terminal plan-review poll (`status:\"passed\"`, `verdict:\"BLOCK\"`) did not prove that the readable `REVIEW_RESULT` belonged to that same run. A caller reading \"latest findings\" could silently consume a prior run's findings.\n\nObserved 2026-09-01 on ticket `549b-9cc5-940e-46c3`: job `1788326596882647223-94573cf0d90d404e87c74855306c16f2` reported terminal BLOCK while the newest readable sidecar was prior-run file `1788325963941841589-...-REVIEW_RESULT.json`; the current sidecar `1788327281362056852-...-REVIEW_RESULT.json` appeared later.\n\n## Root cause / actual layer\n\n`review_plan()` already calls `sidecar.emit()` before `_spawn_gate_daemon()` records the terminal `.rebar/gate_runs/<job_id>` entry. The defect is not a simple in-process order inversion; it is missing per-run sidecar identity:\n\n- `sidecar.emit()` was best-effort and returned only a bool.\n- `_spawn_gate_daemon()` discarded sidecar outcome/identity when writing the terminal run index.\n- `gate_run_status()` reported terminal status plus attestation currency only. For BLOCK, the attestation is unsigned by definition, so `durable` cannot prove findings readiness.\n- `sidecar.latest_review_result(ticket)` is newest-by-ticket, not job-scoped.\n\nThus a terminal run without an exact sidecar receipt cannot distinguish current findings from stale latest findings, an unreadable tracker view, a legacy index, or permanent sidecar failure.\n\n## Fix plan\n\nAdd an exact receipt while preserving existing contracts.\n\n1. `_commands._seam.append_event()` returns the event-envelope timestamp as an additive receipt; existing callers may ignore it.\n2. `plan_review.sidecar.emit()` still returns bool, and also stamps `verdict[\"sidecar_reviewed_at\"]` with the timestamp returned by `append_event()`.\n3. `plan_review.__init__` keeps `verdict[\"sidecar_emitted\"]` boolean semantics unchanged while carrying that stamped receipt on the verdict.\n4. `_mcp_llm._spawn_gate_daemon()` copies `sidecar_emitted` and the exact `sidecar_reviewed_at` from the completed review result into the terminal run index.\n5. `gate_status(job_id)` adds `findings` for plan-review jobs: `sidecar_type`, `readable`, `reason`, `reviewed_at`, `latest_reviewed_at`, and legacy diagnostic `job_started_at`.\n6. `findings.readable=true` only when a file with the exact `sidecar_reviewed_at` prefix exists and parses as a supported `plan_review_result_v1/v2` payload. It never infers freshness from newest timestamp or job start time.\n\nDisposition: `sidecar-not-emitted` and `review-result-generation-unknown` are terminal-unavailable findings states. `review-result-sidecar-missing` is explicitly not-readable for an expected receipt missing from this reader's tracker view; callers may keep polling only under their normal bounded wait policy, and must not read latest findings while it is false. `run-<status>` is the non-terminal keep-polling state.\n\n## Scope / file impact\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py`: additive timestamp return from `append_event()`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py`: stamp `sidecar_reviewed_at` while preserving bool return.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py`: verified call site; bool `sidecar_emitted` remains unchanged.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`: store the exact completed-review receipt in the terminal async run index.\n- `src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py`: compute the plan-review `findings` readability block.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_models.py`, `src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_verdict.schema.json`: document/model additive fields.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py` and `tests/interfaces/store/test_sidecar_reader.py`: regression and receipt tests.\n- `AGENTS.md`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/mcp-reference.md`: document waiting for `findings.readable` before reading findings.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Seed an old `REVIEW_RESULT`, record a terminal newer run with expected `sidecar_reviewed_at`, omit that sidecar, and assert `gate_status` is terminal with `findings.readable=false`, `reason=\"review-result-sidecar-missing\"`.\n- [ ] Write the expected current sidecar and assert the same job reports `findings.readable=true` with `reason=\"current-review-result-sidecar\"`.\n- [ ] Drive two successive runs and assert poll-then-read returns no findings for the newer job until that job's exact sidecar is readable.\n- [ ] Assert terminal `sidecar_emitted=false` reports `findings.readable=false` and `reason=\"sidecar-not-emitted\"`.\n- [ ] Assert the daemon records the exact receipt returned by `review_plan()` even when a newer same-ticket sidecar is already readable.\n- [ ] Assert legacy terminal records without a receipt report `findings.readable=false`, `reason=\"review-result-generation-unknown\"`, with `job_started_at` diagnostic only.\n- [ ] Assert non-terminal plan-review runs report `findings.readable=false`, `reason=\"run-<status>\"`, and `reviewed_at=null`.\n- [ ] Validate with targeted pytest, MCP schema coverage, `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `make test`.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Changing verdict computation or whether a BLOCK is a completed (`passed`) gate run.\n- Making `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecars required for the verdict; they remain best-effort observability.\n- Changing `plan_review_status` or signed-attestation currency.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788363003315305001,"uuid":"b94ad2b0-7b90-42d2-ab03-38ee0d675d6b"}